results/
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
submission/
sample_submission/
baseline.joblib
# Per-salt fits, written when FUSION_ARTIFACT points somewhere else — each is a whole pipeline
# (PCA, scaler, coil gains, models) and they are hundreds of megabytes together.
baseline_*.joblib

# Decoded shots, rebuilt on demand — see my_experiments/shot_cache.py. Tens of GB, and keyed by
# the source parquet's mtime, so it is worthless to anyone else's checkout.
.shot_cache/
# A9's per-frame functionals, one npz per split — see my_experiments/aux_targets.py. About 30 MB
# each and 13 core-hours to rebuild, but keyed by the exact file list, so a checkout with a
# different split cannot use them. Missed when A9 was built; a full per-salt set is ~600 MB.
.aux_targets/

# Your Hugging Face read token, included by the Makefile. .env.example is the tracked stub.
.env

# push_predictions.py writes your scoped HF read token into manifest.json and zips it here.
# Submitted on purpose, but never committed.
submissions/
submission_pointer.zip
manifest.json

# Every run tees its output here, named by UTC timestamp. Watchable while it happens, and not
# worth versioning: tqdm's carriage returns push a production run past a megabyte.
logs/

# Fitted artifacts. `baseline_*.joblib` was already covered, which is the naming the lanes now use
# (one per salt AND arm, so a mega-blend can be assembled with no extra training) — but the older
# per-lane names and the tail-noise pair were not, and they are 14 MB each. None of this belongs in
# a public fork: every one is reproducible from params.yaml plus a salt.
artefacts/lanes/
artefacts/tailnoise/
artefacts/mega/
artefacts/cos/
artefacts/laneB/
artefacts/laneF/
